{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אשה כי תזריע", :translit "isha ki tazria", :gloss "a woman when she conceives"} {:he "והתקדשתם", :translit "u-hitkadishtem", :gloss "and you shall sanctify yourselves"} {:he "אל תשקצו את נפשותיכם", :translit "al tishketzu et nafshotekhem", :gloss "do not make yourselves abominable"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut) of Lev 11:44 to Lev 12:2 drives the legal inference"}], :frame {:text "The prohibition against wasting seed is derived from Leviticus 11:43, 'do not make yourselves abominable,' which is interpreted to forbid bringing impurity upon oneself through improper emission of seed (Niddah 13a). The requirement to sanctify oneself at the time of relations, stated in Leviticus 11:44, is applied by Rabbi to one's conduct in intimacy (Shabbat 86a). The advisory that one who has relieved himself should not immediately engage in relations reflects a concern for bodily purity (Berakhot 22a–b, treating the need for hand-washing and bodily care after using the privy).", :sources ["Niddah 13a" "Shabbat 86a" "Berakhot 22a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "להבדיל בין הטמא ובין הטהור", :translit "le-havdil bein ha-tamei u-vein ha-tahor", :gloss "to distinguish between the unclean and the clean"} {:he "אשה כי תזריע", :translit "isha ki tazria", :gloss "a woman when she conceives"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut) of Lev 11:47 to Lev 12:2 yields the three-month practice and the period-adjacency rule"}], :frame {:text "The practice of waiting three months before resuming relations after marriage or separation is to determine paternity, distinguishing whether a child conceived derives from the first or second husband (Yevamot 100b–101a). Separating from one's wife near her expected menstrual period is a precaution against relations during menstruation, which is forbidden (Leviticus 18:19; Niddah 16a).", :sources ["Yevamot 100b" "Leviticus 18:19" "Niddah 16a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "זכר", :translit "zakhar", :gloss "male"} {:he "ברכה", :translit "berakhah", :gloss "blessing"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "זכר", :b "ברכה"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "וטמאה שבעת ימים", :translit "u-tme'ah shiv'at yamim", :gloss "and she is unclean seven days"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Parallel drawn between the seven days of postpartum impurity and the seven days of mourning"}], :frame {:text "The seven-day period of impurity after bearing a male child is stated at Leviticus 12:2. The seven days of mourning established for all relatives are traced back to the seven days of mourning observed by Job's friends, as related in Job 2:13 (Mo'ed Katan 20a).", :sources ["Leviticus 12:2" "Job 2:13" "Mo'ed Katan 20a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut) of Lev 11:44 to Lev 12:2 drives the legal inference", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut) of Lev 11:47 to Lev 12:2 yields the three-month practice and the period-adjacency rule", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "זכר", :a-value 227, :b "ברכה", :b-value 227, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :other, :note "Parallel drawn between the seven days of postpartum impurity and the seven days of mourning", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:23:07.204680917Z", :model "glm-5.2"}